---
/**
 * The starfield that sits behind every page.
 *
 * A <picture> with a media-scoped <source> so the preload scanner only ever
 * fetches one SVG — a display:none pair on plain <img>s still downloads both.
 *
 * fetchpriority="high" on the <img> raises that one request out of the default
 * priority images start at, where it queues behind the render-blocking
 * stylesheets. It belongs on the <img>, not the <source>: the <source> only
 * chooses the URL, and the <img> is the element that carries the request and
 * every attribute governing it. The hint applies to whichever variant the
 * media query selected, so it does not reintroduce the second download.
 *
 * The paths are absolute because this renders on `/` and on
 * `/articles/<slug>/` alike, and the site is published at an apex domain with
 * no base path (see astro.config.mjs).
 *
 * Styling lives in public/assets/sky.css, not in a <style> block here: this
 * component renders on the landing, whose one inline style block is pinned by
 * a SHA-256 hash in its CSP, and a plain same-origin file behaves the same in
 * `astro dev` as in a build. Same reasoning as article.css and posts.css.
 */
---

<picture class="sky-wrap">
  <source srcset="/assets/starfield-desktop.svg" media="(min-width: 640px)" />
  <img
    class="sky"
    src="/assets/starfield-mobile.svg"
    alt=""
    aria-hidden="true"
    fetchpriority="high"
  />
</picture>
